--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Description:
libnvds_batch_jpegenc.so encodes object images in a batch. It is used by
DeepStream object-encoding helpers.
Refer to the DeepStream SDK documentation for more details.

This software is based in part on the work of the Independent JPEG Group.
The JPEG headers under tegra/ (IJG libjpeg with NVIDIA Tegra acceleration
additions) and oss/ (libjpeg-turbo 1.5.2) are distributed under the IJG
License; see README.ijg and the repository's THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Pre-requisites:
- libnvds_meta.so, libnvbufsurface.so, and libnvbufsurftransform.so
- libglib2.0 Development package
- CUDA Runtime

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Compiling and installing the library:

  $ export CUDA_VER=13.2 # x86, Jetson and SBSA. For IGX Thor, CUDA_VER=13.0
  $ make && sudo -E make install

Skip sudo when already root (for example inside a container).

The library libnvds_batch_jpegenc.so is installed at
/opt/nvidia/deepstream/deepstream/lib/
